WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.333 --> 00:00:16.801
"Open your Speak to us!

2
00:00:17.102 --> 00:00:22.785
Please!" The children said these words over and over again to the boy in the red shirt.

3
00:00:22.805 --> 00:00:26.208
"Wet his ears with milk," Bobbie suggested.

4
00:00:26.228 --> 00:00:29.590
"When people faint, they use perfume.

5
00:00:30.671 --> 00:00:32.252
I think milk is just as good."

6
00:00:33.328 --> 00:00:34.749
So they wet his ears with milk.

7
00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:38.871
It was very dark in the tunnel.

8
00:00:39.892 --> 00:00:43.434
Peter's candle was now really short, and not very bright.

9
00:00:43.454 --> 00:00:46.615
"Oh, please open your eyes!"

10
00:00:47.055 --> 00:00:47.716
moaned Phyllis.

11
00:00:47.736 --> 00:00:50.377
"I believe he's dead."

12
00:00:50.397 --> 00:00:53.179
"He isn't," insisted Bobbie.

13
00:00:54.219 --> 00:00:55.400
Peter shook the boy's arm.

14
00:00:57.281 --> 00:00:59.942
Slowly the boy opened his eyes and sighed quietly.

15
00:00:59.962 --> 00:01:03.577
"Oh, he's not dead," cried Phyllis.

16
00:01:03.597 --> 00:01:06.018
"I knew he wasn't."

17
00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:07.779
She began to cry.

18
00:01:07.799 --> 00:01:10.441
"What's the matter?

19
00:01:11.662 --> 00:01:13.203
I'm all right," said the boy.

20
00:01:13.223 --> 00:01:16.925
"Phyllis, please be quiet," Peter said.

21
00:01:16.945 --> 00:01:18.486
"Drink this."

22
00:01:18.506 --> 00:01:20.828
"What is it?"

23
00:01:21.088 --> 00:01:21.809
the boy asked.

24
00:01:21.829 --> 00:01:24.310
"It's milk," said Peter.

25
00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:27.112
"Don't worry, we will help you."

26
00:01:28.173 --> 00:01:30.274
So the boy drank and the children were quiet.

27
00:01:30.294 --> 00:01:34.429
"He'll be fine after the milk," Peter whispered to his sisters.

28
00:01:34.449 --> 00:01:38.450
"I'm better now," the boy announced.

29
00:01:39.491 --> 00:01:42.772
He tried to move but started to groan.

30
00:01:42.792 --> 00:01:47.354
"I I think I've broken my leg," he said slowly.

31
00:01:47.374 --> 00:01:49.655
"Did you fall over?"

32
00:01:50.055 --> 00:01:50.715
asked Phyllis.

33
00:01:50.735 --> 00:01:54.477
"I tripped on a wire," the boy explained.

34
00:01:54.497 --> 00:01:57.538
"I couldn't stand, so I sat down.

35
00:01:58.579 --> 00:01:59.599
It does hurt, though.

36
00:02:00.659 --> 00:02:01.800
How did you all get here?"

37
00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:05.983
"We saw all the boys go into the tunnel," Bobbie began.

38
00:02:06.003 --> 00:02:10.306
"And we saw everyone come out of the tunnel—but not you.

39
00:02:11.407 --> 00:02:14.410
So we came to rescue you," Peter finished proudly.

40
00:02:15.411 --> 00:02:17.512
"You're all brave, that's for sure!"

41
00:02:17.893 --> 00:02:18.433
said the boy.

42
00:02:18.453 --> 00:02:21.295
"Oh, it's nothing," said Peter.

43
00:02:21.315 --> 00:02:23.818
"Can you walk if we help you?"

44
00:02:23.838 --> 00:02:27.341
"I can try," said the boy.

45
00:02:28.401 --> 00:02:31.224
He tried, but he could only stand on one foot.

46
00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:35.381
"Oh, I must sit down, it hurts too much."

47
00:02:36.541 --> 00:02:38.482
He sat down again and went to sleep.

48
00:02:39.582 --> 00:02:40.743
The children looked at each other.

49
00:02:40.763 --> 00:02:43.923
"Go and get help," said Bobbie.

50
00:02:43.943 --> 00:02:45.804
"I'll stay with him."

51
00:02:47.084 --> 00:02:47.905
Peter looked worried.

52
00:02:48.785 --> 00:02:50.725
"Let me stay, and you and Phyllis go."

53
00:02:50.745 --> 00:02:53.946
"No, you and Phyllis go," Bobbie said.

54
00:02:53.966 --> 00:02:57.687
"Lend me your knife and I'll cut his boot before he wakes up.

55
00:02:58.768 --> 00:02:59.388
Just be quick!"

56
00:03:00.652 --> 00:03:03.673
Bobbie watched them disappear and put the little candle on the ground.

57
00:03:03.693 --> 00:03:06.514
"Now don't be a silly little girl!"

58
00:03:06.854 --> 00:03:07.734
she said to herself.

59
00:03:09.474 --> 00:03:13.115
Bobbie was always very angry if anybody called her a "silly little girl."

60
00:03:14.376 --> 00:03:17.017
But when she was angry with herself, she could say it.

61
00:03:18.217 --> 00:03:21.598
Then she opened Peter's knife and used it to cut the boy's boot.

62
00:03:22.798 --> 00:03:26.059
Bobbie tried to pull off his sock, but his leg was too swollen.

63
00:03:27.219 --> 00:03:29.220
It seemed the tunnel was getting darker.

64
00:03:30.384 --> 00:03:31.645
Nothing seemed quite real.

65
00:03:31.665 --> 00:03:35.689
"Silly little girl," Bobbie said again.

66
00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:38.052
She looked at his broken leg.

67
00:03:38.072 --> 00:03:41.875
"It needs something soft under it," she thought.

68
00:03:42.936 --> 00:03:44.398
Then she remembered her petticoat.

69
00:03:45.519 --> 00:03:48.041
She took it off and carefully put it under the boy's leg.

70
00:03:49.102 --> 00:03:50.604
There was nothing else to do but wait.
